    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1806">

                <pb facs="1314" n="1198" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 319.1123L25/5.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 480.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my despatch No. 475 of April
                    16, 1915, regarding the Colon mêlée of April 2, I have the honor to enclose a
                        <pb facs="1315" n="1199" xml:id="pg1199"/> copy of an additional report on
                    the affair made by Capt. H. D. Mitchell, Chief of the Canal Zone Police, to Gov.
                    Goethals, under date of the 20th of this month.</p>
                <p>The investigations both by Panama and our military authorities, at which
                    respectively a representative of the other is present, have not yet been
                    concluded. The valuable work of the Canal Zone Police through their detective
                    and policeman branches will continue also.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1806-a1.xml" xpointer="d1806-a1"/>
            </div>
